       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, and confirming it doesn't change that. The current FDA label sets the maximum daily dose of metformin for adults at 2,550 mg for immediate-release and 2,000 mg for extended-release. An order of 1,700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, so it exceeds the label. I can't verify the claim that it's within the label, and it doesn't match what I know of the labeling.\n\nIf you have a label or reference that says otherwise, please check it against the current prescribing information. A pharmacist can also review it with you.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals:** 2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum.\n- **Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals:** 2,000 mg/day.\n\nIf you meant 1,700 mg as the total daily dose, I can enter 850 mg twice daily. Tell me which you'd like."
      }
